## Usage

`TxDistortionWave` overlays a transparent WebGL2 refraction pass over live DOM, launching a chromatic lens wave with progressive blur from the pressed control to reveal `#revealed`. Without WebGL2 or under reduced motion, it falls back cleanly to a crossfade.

### View transition and wave direction

Pressing Confirm launches a wave from the button that leans toward the click point; controls placed in `#overlay` stay sharp and interactive above the wave.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DistortionWaveBasicDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'
  import { TxDistortionWave } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/distortion-wave'

  const sent = ref(false)
  const triggerRef = ref<HTMLButtonElement | null>(null)
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDistortionWave
      :revealed="sent"
      :source="triggerRef"
      type="vertical"
      palette="colorful"
      :corner-radius="24"
    >
      <div class="review-card">Review transfer</div>
      <template #revealed>
        <div class="receipt-card">Transfer sent</div>
      </template>
      <template #overlay>
        <button ref="triggerRef" type="button" @click="sent = !sent">
          {{ sent ? 'Done' : 'Confirm' }}
        </button>
      </template>
    </TxDistortionWave>
  </template>
---
:::

### Center ring and progress scrubbing

`type="center"` radiates a coloured ring from an avatar or icon while holding the origin sharp; `scrub` freezes any moment between `0` and `1`.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DistortionWaveScrubDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'
  import { TxDistortionWave } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/distortion-wave'

  const scrub = ref<number | null>(0.3)
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDistortionWave type="center" palette="green" :scrub="scrub">
      <div>Pending verification</div>
      <template #revealed>
        <div>Verified</div>
      </template>
    </TxDistortionWave>
  </template>
---
:::

### Best Practices

- Give both the default and `#revealed` layers opaque backgrounds so captured snapshots have no transparent bleed.
- Place trigger buttons, spinners, or live media in `#overlay` so they remain unbent and clickable throughout the wave.
- Cross-origin images and webfonts need CORS headers to appear in the refracted snapshot; iframes are skipped.
- Drive transitions by toggling `:revealed` rather than unmounting the component with `v-if`.

## API Reference

### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `revealed` | `boolean` | — | Controlled view state; `true` advances the wave, `false` collapses it back. |
| `type` | `'vertical' \| 'horizontal' \| 'center'` | `'vertical'` | Wave front geometry, each with tuned physics defaults. |
| `source` | `Element \| Ref<Element \| null> \| Rect \| null` | Last pressed control | Origin element, template ref, or local rectangle for the wave. |
| `focus` | `{ x: number; y: number } \| null` | Last pointer press | Local point the front leans toward as it launches. |
| `palette` | `'colorful' \| 'green' \| 'ocean' \| 'sunset' \| 'mono' \| string \| DistortionWavePalette` | By `type` | Built-in palette name, single hex colour, or custom palette object. |
| `waveStyle` | `DistortionWaveStyleInput` | — | Fine-grained timing, lens, blur, rim, and particle overrides. |
| `scale` | `number \| 'auto'` | `'auto'` | CSS pixels per logical point; `'auto'` scales proportionally to the host. |
| `cornerRadius` | `number` | Host `border-radius` | Corner radius followed by the edge colour rim in CSS pixels. |
| `scrub` | `number \| null` | — | Holds the wave at progress `0–1` when set; `null` resumes playback. |
| `capture` | `boolean \| DistortionWaveCaptureFunction` | `true` | Captures live DOM into textures for lens bending; `false` draws colour only. |
| `live` | `boolean \| 'animations'` | `true` | Automatically refreshes cached view snapshots after DOM mutations. |
| `prewarm` | `boolean` | `true` | Captures initial snapshot on idle after mount so the first wave starts immediately. |
| `resolution` | `number` | Device DPR | Canvas backing pixel ratio per CSS pixel. |
| `reducedMotion` | `'system' \| 'always' \| 'never'` | `'system'` | Reduced-motion policy; crossfades instead of running the wave when active. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `finish` | `revealed: boolean` | Fired when a wave settles onto a view; skipped if reversed mid-flight. |

### Slots

| Slot | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `default` | Initial view shown when `revealed` is `false`. |
| `revealed` | Target view revealed behind the wave; omit to sweep across the same view. |
| `overlay` | Unbent live controls layered above the WebGL canvas. |

### Exposed Methods

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `play(options?)` | Runs a forward wave imperatively. |
| `reverse()` | Collapses the wave back to the first view. |
| `reset()` | Immediately restores the initial view without animation. |
| `prepare()` | Captures fresh view textures immediately and returns a Promise. |

## Overview

- Both views share a single CSS Grid cell sized to the larger layer, preventing layout shifts mid-transition.
- The transparent WebGL2 canvas only owns pixels actively bent or tinted by the wave and releases idle GPU textures automatically after rest.
- Without WebGL2 or under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, the component switches via a short crossfade and still emits `finish`.

